### ArrayList.Sort Method
Here is an example of how you can specify constraints on the ArrayList.Sort method's parameters:

```csharp
[PexMethod]
public void Sort([PexAssumeValid]ArrayList arrList)
{
    AssumePrecondition.IsTrue(arrList.Count > 0);

    arrList.Sort();

    for (int i = 0; i < arrList.Count - 1; i++)
    {
        PexObserve.ValueForViewing("$arrList[" + i + "]", arrList[i]);
        Debug.Assert(arrList[i] <= arrList[i + 1]);
    }
}
```

The above contract test ensures that the ArrayList arrList is a valid ArrayList with at least one element. Then, by calling the Sort method, it sorts all items in arrList. It then checks for each item (i) in arrList if it is lesser than or equal to the next item (arrList[i + 1]).

Please note that the [PexObserve.ValueForViewing](https://research.microsoft.com/en-us/um/cambridge/projects/static-analysis-tools-for-net-2010/Binaries/p1020.pdf) method is used to observe the values in the array list, it allows you to see the array list values during the testing process.

By using these constraints, we can make a series of automated tests to ensure the correct functionality of the ArrayList class.

***Important Note*** 

Do use PEX (Pex) on a test project whenever you are testing a production code, it is important that your test should replicate a real usage scenario for your target methods to ensure every feature is tested effectively.

Please note that Microsoft's PEX tool has a limitation to handle maximum 1024 elements in the ArrayList. If you have more than 1024 elements in the list then you may have to use other tools for test generation.

**References:**

- Microsoft Research's [Static Analysis Tools for .NET 2010](https://research.microsoft.com/en-us/um/cambridge/projects/static-analysis-tools-for-net-2010/) site.
- [Code Contracts for .NET by Microsoft Research](http://research.microsoft.com/en-us/projects/contracts/default.aspx)
- [Code Contracts: A Power Tool for Code Quality](http://www.codeproject.com/Articles/418364/Code-Contracts-A-Power-Tool-for-Code-Quality)
- [ArrayList Class (System.Collections)](https://msdn.microsoft.com/en-us/library/c6hyw2k4.aspx)




































































































































